WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.128
Hi, I'm Rocket!

00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:05.478
Decision models like Jev pick an answer from a list you send.

00:00:05.478 --> 00:00:08.828
Here's what that shape rules out, and what it only seems to.

00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:14.315
A generative model's output is its vocabulary, sampled again and again.

00:00:14.315 --> 00:00:18.505
A decision model's output is one item from the list you sent.

00:00:19.858 --> 00:00:21.827
Why can't it write a string, or plan?

00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:22.566
Count the output.

00:00:22.986 --> 00:00:25.940
A Choice carries at most two hundred and fifty-five options.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.350
So one call returns about eight bits.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.044
No text, and no scratchpad to carry a plan into the next call.

00:00:33.858 --> 00:00:36.399
Score each option alone, and order can't matter.

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:39.893
But a question that spans two options has nothing to find.

00:00:39.893 --> 00:00:41.799
Jev scores zero of a hundred.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:45.895
Share one context, and relational questions become at least answerable.

00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:51.040
But position gets a prior: slot A is worth about one point seven logits.

00:00:52.525 --> 00:00:54.266
So the limits are a specification.

00:00:54.266 --> 00:00:56.298
The vendor's own docs give the rule.

00:00:56.718 --> 00:01:02.155
Something enumerates a finite answer set: a regex, the page's tools, a component catalog.

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:05.474
The model picks within it, so it can't invent a value

00:01:05.474 --> 00:01:06.528
or transpose a digit.

00:01:06.948 --> 00:01:09.968
Then code, or a generative model, composes the result.

00:01:11.142 --> 00:01:14.782
Put the bounded model where the answer set is already finite, and

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:16.601
where something else owns the composition.

00:01:19.192 --> 00:01:24.411
To recap: one option out, two opposite prices, and a rule: enumerate, decide, compose.

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:26.863
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:26.863 --> 00:01:27.443
I'm Rocket.

00:01:27.443 --> 00:01:27.733
Bye!
